# `minio/mint` is archived and its `edge` tag is a moving target, so s3s runs
# the suite from an image it controls: s3s-project/mint builds the archived mint
# with the SDK revisions pinned and fixes the client-side test defects the image
# used to fail on: the conditional copy in minio-js reads a field the SDK does
# not return, and minio-js, minio-java and aws-sdk-ruby put an unsigned
# `x-amz-acl` on a presigned PUT, which AWS and s3s refuse - plus a fix for the
# mc download host that no longer exists. It also carries the `patches/` series
# applied on top of the upstream tests: 0005 makes the `aws-sdk-go-v2`
# conditional-delete case expect `NoSuchKey` for `If-Match: *` on a missing key,
# which is what Amazon S3 answers; 0006 runs the `aws-sdk-java-v2` cases over
# plaintext behind `ENABLE_HTTP_TESTS`, which `scripts/mint.sh` sets, so the suite
# logs its seven lines here instead of nothing at all; and 0007 gives that suite's
# CRT case an object it can range over, because a range request against a zero
# byte object cannot be satisfied. The image is amd64 only.
# Override `MINT_IMAGE_REF` to test another build.
MINT_IMAGE_REF="${MINT_IMAGE_REF:-ghcr.io/s3s-project/mint:202610061654@sha256:60cf8e310d9376cff7dedc10761c34b835397c8f22174ce033232dae2614cf2f}"
